This is a config review needing describe_trails, get_trail_status, and get_event_selectors, which falls under the rule that CloudTrail questions always get delegated. I'll explain my plan to the user, then hand this off to a subagent to check the trail config and related S3/KMS/CloudWatch/SNS resources via use_aws as a fallback.

"}]}

{"id": "938571c1-fd12-4346-b64b-b8170077d3e9", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll review the trail's configuration: scope, event selectors, delivery and integrity settings, and its status. Then I'll list the visibility gaps.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_qBETXIgg06g3rNPYomcgqA", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "trail-visibility-review", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes", "verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Review the AWS CloudTrail trail named 'nebula-single-region-trail' and identify its visibility/logging gaps.",
  "context": "The user wants a configuration audit of this trail (not an incident investigation). Start in account 012345678901, region us-east-1 (the agent space's account/region); if the trail isn't found there, check other regions and associated accounts via list_associations. Use read-only calls only. CloudTrail control-plane describe/get calls via use_aws may be blocked; if so, use the CloudTrail route from the investigating-infrastructure-changes skill and fall back to inspecting related resources (S3 bucket, KMS key, CloudWatch Logs log group, SNS, other trails, EventBridge/Config) via use_aws.",
  "resources": ["nebula-single-region-trail"],
  "criteria": "Determine and report: IsMultiRegionTrail; home region; IncludeGlobalServiceEvents; IsOrganizationTrail; management events (read/write, excluded sources such as KMS/RDS Data API); basic vs advanced event selectors; data events configured (S3 object-level, Lambda invoke, DynamoDB, others) and which resources/buckets are covered; Insights events enabled; log file validation; SSE-KMS encryption; CloudWatch Logs integration and metric filters/alarms; SNS notifications; S3 delivery bucket settings (versioning, MFA delete, object lock, lifecycle/retention, public access block, access logging, cross-account/replication); trail logging status (IsLogging, latest delivery errors, latest delivery/digest time, gaps/stop-logging history); whether other trails in the account cover other regions or compensate; and which regions have no coverage. Return a concise prioritized list of gaps (high/medium/low) with the evidence for each, and clearly state anything you could not verify and why. Shallow pass."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit CloudTrail trail configuration for visibility gaps"}], "created_at": null}

